,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kachama-Ganjule language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kachama-Ganjule_language,Language family. Afro-Asiatic.Kachama-Ganjule is an Afroasiatic language spoken in Ethiopia on islands in Lake Chamo and Lake Abaya.,Kachama-Ganjule,Afro-Asiatic
1,Kachama-Ganjule Language (KCX)... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kcx/,Kachama-Ganjule is a stable indigenous language of Ethiopia. It belongs to the Afro-Asiatic language family.,Kachama-Ganjule,Afro-Asiatic
2,Kachama-Ganjule - kcx (Afro-Asiatic) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/kcx/,"Kachama-Ganjule (kcx) is part of the Afro-Asiatic family and Afro-Asiatic, Omotic, North, Gonga-Gimojan, Gimojan, Ometo-Gimira, Ometo, East class. Kachama-Ganjule speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts",Kachama-Ganjule,Afro-Asiatic
3,Kachama-Ganjule,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Kachama-Ganjule.htm,Other comments: Kachama-Ganjule has a decimal system of counting similar to that of Zayse-Zargulla. The linker -ne in the compound numbers means 'and'. The number for 'thousand' is borrowed from Amharic. The above data was taken from Ganjule dialect.,Kachama-Ganjule,Afro-Asiatic
4,Category:Kachama-Ganjule terms derived from Afroasiatic...,https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Kachama-Ganjule_terms_derived_from_Afroasiatic_languages,"Kachama-Ganjule terms that originate from one of the Afroasiatic languages. This category should, ideally, contain only other categories. Entries can be categorized here, too, when the proper subcategory is unclear.",Kachama-Ganjule,Afro-Asiatic
5,Afro-Asiatic Languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/afro-asiatic-languages/,"Information concerning Afro-Asiatic Languages Where are Afro-Asiatic languages spoken? These languages are spoken in a vast trans-continental geographical area. In Africa, they are spoken across the North of the continent, from Ethiopia in the East to Mauritania in the West.",Kachama-Ganjule,Afro-Asiatic
6,Microsoft Word - TABLE OF CONTEN1.doc,https://theswissbay.ch/pdf/Books/Linguistics/Mega+linguistics+pack/Afro-Asiatic/Omotic/Kachama-Ganjule;+A+Grammar+of+Haro+(Woldemariam).pdf,"The Ganjule, who used to live on an island of Lake Chamo, currently inhabit the village of Shele-Mela, west of Lake Chamo, some 15 kilometres south of Arba Minch, on the main road to Konso. The population of the Gatsame and Ganjule is estimated to be 1000 and 800, respectively.",Kachama-Ganjule,Afro-Asiatic
7,Endangered Languages Project - Gats'amé,https://www.endangeredlanguages.com/lang/4358,"Also known as. Kachama-Ganjule, Gats'ame, Get'eme, Gatame, Haruro, Gidicho, Kachama, Gatsame, Qechem. CLASSIFICATION. Afro-Asiatic, Omotic, Ometo. Code authority. Iso 639-3.",Kachama-Ganjule,Afro-Asiatic
